    "derived_on_behalf_of": "ZeroBook",
    "hsn_bifurcation_start_fp": "n/a (GSTR-3B has no HSN section)",
    "caveats": [
      "The utility zero-fills ALL 5 sup_details objects with the full {txval,iamt,camt,samt,csamt} set rather than trimming osup_zero/osup_nil_exmp/osup_nongst as the portal schema does.",
      "eco_reg_sup (3.1.1(ii)) emits ONLY txval (omits iamt/camt/samt/csamt).",
      "ltfee_details emits ONLY {camt, samt} (omits iamt and csamt).",
      "inter_sup arrays (unreg_details/comp_details/uin_details) each emit ONLY {pos, txval, iamt} (iamt only, inter-state).",
      "itc_net is an OBJECT {iamt,camt,samt,csamt}; itc_avl/itc_rev/itc_inelg are ARRAYS of {ty,...}. No txval anywhere under itc_elg.",
      "Top-level key order is gstin, ret_period, sup_details, eco_dtls, itc_elg, inward_sup, intr_ltfee, inter_sup — inter_sup (Table 3.2) is emitted LAST, after intr_ltfee, not adjacent to sup_details.",
      "Modest string-extraction caveat: sup_details' single shared money-key literal block is consistent with a loop that writes all 5 keys to every object; a per-object conditional skip cannot be 100% excluded from the string dump alone, but no trimmed variant appears.",
      "Extractor and independent verifier both reported HIGH confidence; the verifier reproduced the exact literal stream and offsets."
    ]
  },
